# LOCATE — "a compass that finds villages". Points him at the nearest place of a kind.
#
# Finding it is Java's (Locate): the search is vanilla's own /locate, which a function cannot run and
# still hand the answer to a compass. This only asks, by tagging him, and makes it heard; Locate puts
# the real compass on the place (lodestone_tracker), tells him how far, and draws the way in sparkles.
function effect()
    /execute as ${TARGET} run tag @s add mfam_locate_${PLACE}
    /playsound minecraft:item.lodestone_compass.lock master @a ~ ~ ~ 1 1.2
end
